WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.315
Lesson 10.5.

00:00:02.315 --> 00:00:04.910
Active concentrated-liquidity management.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.249
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:07.249 --> 00:00:09.755
to choose a range width and a rebalance rule

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:11.815
that fee income can actually pay for.

00:00:13.115 --> 00:00:14.405
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:16.090
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.805
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.805 --> 00:00:20.330
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.492
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:28.877
Narrower ranges earn more fees per

00:00:28.877 --> 00:00:35.502
dollar while in range and go out of

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:42.524
range sooner. the calculator Every rebalance costs

00:00:42.524 --> 00:00:46.542
gas and swap fees and locks

00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:50.474
in the impermanent loss so

00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:54.997
far. Professionals set a rule

00:00:54.997 --> 00:01:00.176
before entering: $2,400–$3,600 (±20%): ~10.4×. $2,700–$3,300

00:01:00.176 --> 00:01:03.911
(±10%): ~20.4×. $2,850–$3,150 (±5%): ~40.5×.

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:07.726
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:07.726 --> 00:01:11.726
ETH typically moves ±7% a week.

00:01:11.726 --> 00:01:13.747
A ±5% range would be

00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:16.356
out of range most weeks.

00:01:16.356 --> 00:01:20.904
The rule points to ±10–12%: ~20× efficiency,

00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:23.531
and time in range to earn.

00:01:24.831 --> 00:01:27.430
Trending markets and volatility above what

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.881
the range was sized for.

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:31.641
Here's your checklist.

00:01:31.641 --> 00:01:33.176
Do it now, for real.

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:37.241
First, Width ≥ 1.5× typical weekly move.

00:01:37.241 --> 00:01:40.506
Next, Rebalance trigger and invalidation written.

00:01:40.506 --> 00:01:42.886
Then, Rebalance cost budget set.

00:01:42.886 --> 00:01:46.931
And finally, P&L tracked against holding (Lesson 2.4).

00:01:48.231 --> 00:01:49.441
Question 1.

00:01:49.441 --> 00:01:53.174
Why does a ±5% range earn ~2×

00:01:53.174 --> 00:01:57.156
the fees of ±10% while in range?

00:02:01.576 --> 00:02:04.245
The answer: The same capital is concentrated

00:02:04.245 --> 00:02:06.084
in half the price range, so it

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:08.516
provides about twice the liquidity there.

00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:11.061
Question 2.

00:02:11.061 --> 00:02:12.546
What does a rebalance lock in?

00:02:16.966 --> 00:02:19.910
The answer: The impermanent loss accrued so

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.851
far, plus gas and swap costs.

00:02:23.151 --> 00:02:24.421
Question 3.

00:02:24.421 --> 00:02:27.216
Price breaks structure and exits the range.

00:02:27.216 --> 00:02:28.041
Re-centre?

00:02:32.461 --> 00:02:35.251
The answer: No. That's an invalidation.

00:02:35.251 --> 00:02:36.291
Exit per plan.

00:02:37.591 --> 00:02:40.106
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:40.106 --> 00:02:42.522
Next up, Lesson 10.6: Restaking

00:02:42.522 --> 00:02:45.391
and points: pricing speculative yield.
